-- STATUS, added by the fleet lead on 2026-10-14 (the comments below were written by the independent author and describe the state when it wrote them):
-- of the 14 assertions, 11 (DIS-2 delivery-day timeliness, DIS-3 an extension cannot shorten, DIS-4 reg 4 and the temporary licence, DIS-5 a defective
-- s.42(b) notice) FAILED against the modules as first written, were repaired by G6 and G8, and now PASS. The other 3 (DIS-1, a corporation at a dash on
-- Third Schedule items (1), (2) and (4)) still REFUSE: G6 keeps its fork F-DASH, open question O34. check.sh expects 0 failures and 3 refusals here.

-- ind-c-tests-disagree.l4: assertions that FAIL or REFUSE and that I believe are the encoding's fault.
-- Every assertion here is meant to fail (or refuse) against the snapshot.  None was edited to match the code.
-- Counted: 14 assertions (3 refuse, 11 fail).  Each group says whether its scenario was decided BEFORE the encoding
-- was opened (in work/ind-c/expectations.md) or is a probe written AFTER reading it.

§ `ind-c: disagreements`

§§ `Fixtures`

`no rest days` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS EMPTY

`a corporate violator` MEANS Person WITH `reference for the person` IS "corp-1", `kind of person` IS `a corporation`
`an individual violator` MEANS Person WITH `reference for the person` IS "ind-1", `kind of person` IS `an individual`

GIVEN what IS A `Listed violation`
GIVETH A Violation
`a corporation's violation of` what MEANS
    Violation WITH `the violator` IS `a corporate violator`
                 , `the listed violation` IS what
                 , `reference for the act` IS "act-1"
                 , `date of the act` IS YMD 2027 3 10

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Notice of intention`
`a complete notice delivered on` d MEANS
    `Notice of intention` WITH
        `delivered on` IS d
        `in writing` IS TRUE
        `states the act or omission that is the breach and the date of the breach` IS TRUE
        `states the amount of the sanction` IS TRUE
        `the period for payment the notice states, in days` IS JUST 30
        `states the violator's right to make representations under section 43` IS TRUE
        `states that the notice will be treated as a payment demand if the right is not used` IS TRUE
        `states the power to add for a continuing or repeat violation and the rate of the addition` IS TRUE
        `states the intention to publish the violator's name` IS FALSE

`a warning delivered on 2027-03-01` MEANS
    `Administrative warning` WITH
        `the violator` IS `an individual violator`
        `the listed violation the warning concerns` IS `work with no licence at all`
        `delivered on` IS YMD 2027 3 1
        `states the act or omission that is the breach and the date of the breach` IS TRUE
        `tells the violator to stop the breach` IS TRUE
        `warns of a sanction for a continuing or repeat violation` IS TRUE
        `states the violator's right to ask for cancellation under section 53` IS TRUE
        `cancelled under section 53` IS FALSE

§§ `DIS-1 (decided before; A1, A2, A4): a corporation at a dash may not be sanctioned (3 refuse)`

-- Gazette p. 205 prints a dash in the corporation column of items (1), (2) and (4).  s.41(a) empowers the
-- Commissioner to impose "in the amount set in column B beside it"; where column B sets none there is nothing to
-- impose.  Expected FALSE; the encoding REFUSES (fork F-DASH: "a figure was left out" is its other reading).
#ASSERT NOT (`s 41(a) — a financial sanction may be imposed for` (`a corporation's violation of` `work with no licence at all`) TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 41(a) — a financial sanction may be imposed for` (`a corporation's violation of` `work without a licence of the kind appropriate to the system`) TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 41(a) — a financial sanction may be imposed for` (`a corporation's violation of` `installation without the tightness test of the piping`) TRUE TRUE)

§§ `DIS-2 (probe after opening): an act on the day of delivery is "within N days from" it (5 fail)`

-- s.43: "within 30 days from the time the notice was delivered".  IL s.10(a) leaves the day of delivery out of the
-- COUNT that fixes the last day; it does not make an act on that day untimely.  The encoding asks whether the day is
-- "inside the period beginning on" the day AFTER delivery, so representations made on the day the notice arrives
-- are not "within the period", and s.44(d) then treats the notice as a payment demand although the violator argued.
#ASSERT `s 43 — the day` (YMD 2027 3 1) `is within the period for representations of` (`a complete notice delivered on` (YMD 2027 3 1)) NOTHING `no rest days`
#ASSERT `s 43, s 44(d) — the violator made his representations within the period` (`a complete notice delivered on` (YMD 2027 3 1)) NOTHING `no rest days` (JUST (YMD 2027 3 1))
-- He argued, so there is no deemed demand: the demand day is not yet known (NOTHING), not 2027-03-31.
#ASSERT `s 44 — the day the payment demand is delivered or treated as delivered` (`a complete notice delivered on` (YMD 2027 3 1)) NOTHING (`s 43, s 44(d) — the violator made his representations within the period` (`a complete notice delivered on` (YMD 2027 3 1)) NOTHING `no rest days` (JUST (YMD 2027 3 1))) NOTHING `no rest days` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The same defect in s.53 (a request to cancel on the day the warning arrives) and s.56 (an appeal filed the day the
-- notice of the decision arrives).
#ASSERT `s 53(a) — the day` (YMD 2027 3 1) `is within the period to ask to cancel` `a warning delivered on 2027-03-01` `given` NOTHING `with` `no rest days`
#ASSERT `s 56(a) — the day` (YMD 2027 6 1) `is within the period to appeal that runs from` (YMD 2027 6 1) `with` `no rest days`

§§ `DIS-3 (probe after opening): an "extension" cannot shorten the period (2 fail)`

-- s.43 and s.53(b): the Commissioner "may EXTEND" the period.  An official's day that falls before the end of
-- the 30 days is not an extension; the 30 days stand.  The encoding takes the official's day whatever it is.
#ASSERT `s 43 — the last day for representations` (`a complete notice delivered on` (YMD 2027 3 1)) (JUST (`Extension granted by the Commissioner` WITH `the period now ends on` IS YMD 2027 3 20, `special reasons were recorded` IS TRUE)) `no rest days` EQUALS YMD 2027 3 31
#ASSERT `s 53(a), (b) — the last day to ask to cancel` `a warning delivered on 2027-03-01` `counting from its delivery, given` (JUST (`Extension granted by the Commissioner` WITH `the period now ends on` IS YMD 2027 3 20, `special reasons were recorded` IS TRUE)) `with` `no rest days` EQUALS YMD 2027 3 31

§§ `DIS-4 (probe after opening): reg 4 and the foreign expert's temporary licence (3 fail)`

-- Reg 4: "the Registrar shall not give a licence for which a fee was fixed ... unless the fee was paid in full".
-- Reg 2(d) fixes 398 for the application for the temporary licence.  The encoding's own reading taken is that this
-- fee binds the grant; asked about the application it bars an unpaid grant, but asked about the GRANT (a service it
-- also accepts) it finds no fee and leaves the Registrar free.  Expected: not free, nothing having been paid, in both
-- vintages.
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 4 leaves the Registrar free to give or renew the licence in the vintage` `the Fees Regulations as made` `the service of being granted a foreign expert's temporary licence` 0 (YMD 2025 8 1) EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` `the Fees Regulations as made` `the service of being granted a foreign expert's temporary licence` 0 (YMD 2025 8 1) EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 4 leaves the Registrar free to give or renew the licence in the vintage` `the Fees Regulations as amended` `the service of being granted a foreign expert's temporary licence` 0 (YMD 2026 6 1) EMPTY)

§§ `DIS-5 (probe after opening): a notice without the s.42(b)(3) statements is deemed a payment demand (1 fail)`

-- s.44(d) deems the notice a payment demand when the violator did not argue under s.43; s.42(b)(3) is the statement
-- that tells him of that right and of that consequence.  The encoding reads a notice that omits what s.42(b) requires as
-- no notice under s.42 (fork F-NOTICE), so `s 43 — the violator may make written representations` gives him NO right
-- (FULFILLED) for such a notice; yet s.44 still deems the same notice a payment demand delivered on 2027-03-31.
-- Expected, on the encoding's own reading of s.42: no deemed demand (NOTHING).
`a notice silent on the right to argue` MEANS
    `Notice of intention` WITH
        `delivered on` IS YMD 2027 3 1
        `in writing` IS TRUE
        `states the act or omission that is the breach and the date of the breach` IS TRUE
        `states the amount of the sanction` IS TRUE
        `the period for payment the notice states, in days` IS JUST 30
        `states the violator's right to make representations under section 43` IS FALSE
        `states that the notice will be treated as a payment demand if the right is not used` IS FALSE
        `states the power to add for a continuing or repeat violation and the rate of the addition` IS TRUE
        `states the intention to publish the violator's name` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `s 44 — the day the payment demand is delivered or treated as delivered` `a notice silent on the right to argue` NOTHING FALSE NOTHING `no rest days` EQUALS NOTHING
